# ============================================
# father_behan.dialogue
# ============================================
NPC: father_behan
LOCATION: rectory

TOPIC: sixth_man
  GATE: never
  # Permanently excluded. No line exists for this topic, on this NPC
  # or any other. Do not fill this in on a later pass.

TOPIC: club_five
  GATE: always
  LABEL: "Ask about the five club members"
  BEHAN: "Wexford's temper. Fenn's vanity. Kessler's grudges. Corliss's ambitions.
          I'll discuss any of it. None of it explains a hole above the bridge of a nose."
  CHOICE: "You knew all six."
    BEHAN: "I knew what men tell a priest, which is not the same as what they are.
            Ask your question, Officer. I've answered worse."

TOPIC: club_invitation
  GATE: always
  LABEL: "Ask about the club invitations"
  CHOICE: "You were invited to the club. Twice. You declined both times."
    BEHAN: "I did."
  CHOICE: "Why?"
    BEHAN: [He says nothing further. The silence is not evasive. It is final.]
    NOTEBOOK: "A refusal offered without excuse.
               Walter has learned to trust a plain no more than a decorated one."

TOPIC: bullets
  GATE: always
  LABEL: "Ask about the bullet wound"
  CHOICE: "Have you ever heard of a bullet that leaves no exit wound?"
    BEHAN: [A pause held a beat too long.] "Ask your question, Officer. I've answered worse."
    # deliberately reuses his own stock line — the second use reads as evasion,
    # not repetition, once the player's heard it land honestly once already
